1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Bc5 3. f4 d6 4. Nf3 Bg4 5. h3 Bxf3 6. Qxf3 Nf6 7. Bc4 Nc6 8. d3 Nd4 9. Qg3 Qe7 10. Kd1 Rg8 11. Rf1 O-O-O 12. fxe5 dxe5 13. Bg5 c6 14. Qh4 b5 15. Bb3 a5 16. a3 Nxb3 17. cxb3 Rxd3+ 18. Kc2 Rgd8 ({The ILN gives the unfeasible move 'K to B 2nd' here (presumably a typographical error replicating White's last move). It is not entirely obvious what Black did instead but the reconstruction fits the bill up to a point.} 18... Kc7) 19. Rae1 ({Would White have overlooked the opportunity to play} 19. Nd5 {here? Seems doubtful.}) 19... Bxa3 {"Nearly throwing away a well-won game. Fortunately for Black, his opponent overlooked the correct reply."} 20. bxa3 ({"} 20. Nd5 {certainly wins the exchange, and possibly staves off defeat." However, here it loses.}) 20... Qc5 21. Bc1 Qxc3+ 22. Kb1 Qxb3+ 23. Bb2 Rd2 {Source: Illustrated London News - Saturday 24 June 1911} 0-1

